.SS " nodes\&.document sphinx\&.util\&.docutils\&.new_document (str source_path, Any  settings = \fCNone\fP)"

.PP
.nf
Return a new empty document object\&.  This is an alternative of docutils'\&.

This is a simple wrapper for ``docutils\&.utils\&.new_document()``\&.  It
caches the result of docutils' and use it on second call for instantiation\&.
This makes an instantiation of document nodes much faster\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " Iterator[None] sphinx\&.util\&.docutils\&.patch_docutils (str | os\&.PathLike[str] | None  confdir = \fCNone\fP)"

.PP
.nf
Patch to docutils temporarily\&.
.fi
.PP
 
.SS " Iterator[None] sphinx\&.util\&.docutils\&.patched_get_language ()"

.PP
.nf
Patch docutils\&.languages\&.get_language() temporarily\&.

This ignores the second argument ``reporter`` to suppress warnings\&.
See: https://github\&.com/sphinx-doc/sphinx/issues/3788

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " Iterator[None] sphinx\&.util\&.docutils\&.patched_rst_get_language ()"

.PP
.nf
Patch docutils\&.parsers\&.rst\&.languages\&.get_language()\&.
Starting from docutils 0\&.17, get_language() in ``rst\&.languages``
also has a reporter, which needs to be disabled temporarily\&.

This should also work for old versions of docutils,
because reporter is none by default\&.

See: https://github\&.com/sphinx-doc/sphinx/issues/10179

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " None sphinx\&.util\&.docutils\&.register_directive (str name, type[\fBDirective\fP] directive)"

.PP
.nf
Register a directive to docutils\&.

This modifies global state of docutils\&.  So it is better to use this
inside ``docutils_namespace()`` to prevent side-effects\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " None sphinx\&.util\&.docutils\&.register_node (type[\fBElement\fP] node)"

.PP
.nf
Register a node to docutils\&.

This modifies global state of some visitors\&.  So it is better to use this
inside ``docutils_namespace()`` to prevent side-effects\&.

.fi
.PP
 
